<div id=3D"rank-math-faq" class=3D"rank-math-block">
<div class=3D"rank-math-list " style=3D"content-visibility: auto;contain-in=
trinsic-size: auto 836px;">
<div id=3D"faq-question-1783505204629" class=3D"rank-math-list-item">
<h3 class=3D"rank-math-question ">How to hack a website and change it?</h3>
<div class=3D"rank-math-answer ">

<p>Website attacks commonly exploit weak input validation (SQL injection), =
unsanitized user input (cross-site scripting), stolen or weak credentials, =
misconfigured permissions, or outdated software with known vulnerabilities.=
 Attackers may also use social engineering or phishing to gain access. </p>
<p>Once inside, they can alter content, steal data, or deface pages, highli=
ghting the need for strong security practices.</p>

</div>
</div>
<div id=3D"faq-question-1784083946114" class=3D"rank-math-list-item">
<h3 class=3D"rank-math-question ">What are common website hacking technique=
s?</h3>
<div class=3D"rank-math-answer ">

<p>Common website hacking techniques include SQL injection, XSS, authentica=
tion bypass, file upload abuse, credential stuffing, session hijacking, and=
 misconfigurations. Ethical hackers use these methods in authorized securit=
y tests to identify weaknesses, prioritize fixes, and reduce the risk of re=
al-world attacks.</p>

</div>
</div>
<div id=3D"faq-question-1785271243135" class=3D"rank-math-list-item">
<h3 class=3D"rank-math-question ">How do you stop attackers from crashing a=
 website?</h3>
<div class=3D"rank-math-answer ">

<p>To stop attackers from crashing a website, combine a web application fir=
ewall, DDoS protection, and rate limiting with regular penetration testing.=
 Pentests uncover the exact weaknesses attackers target, like unpatched ser=
vices and resource-heavy endpoints, so you can fix them before they take th=
e site down</p>

</div>
</div>
<div id=3D"faq-question-1785310918474" class=3D"rank-math-list-item">
<h3 class=3D"rank-math-question ">Is hacking a website legal?</h3>
<div class=3D"rank-math-answer ">

<p>Hacking a website without permission is illegal and punishable under law=
s like the CFAA and IT Act. The right path is ethical hacking, where author=
ized penetration testers simulate real attacks on systems they=E2=80=99re a=
llowed to test, helping owners find and fix vulnerabilities before real att=
ackers do.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
